This project, `haskell-halogen-store`, is based on code from the PureScript Halogen Store
library, licensed under MIT, and adapted to GHC Haskell.
See https://github.com/thomashoneyman/purescript-halogen-store for the original project
(Copyright (c) 2020 Thomas Honeyman).

`Halogen.Store.Monad`, `Halogen.Store.Select` and `Halogen.Store.Connect` follow the modules of
the same names: the `MonadStore` class with `getStore`, `updateStore` and `emitSelected`, the
`StoreT` transformer with `runStoreT` and `runAndEmitStoreT`, the `Selector` with `select`,
`selectEq`, `selectAll` and `selectEmitter`, and `Connected`, `connect` and `subscribe` keep their
names and meaning.

It builds on `haskell-halogen-core`, which carries its own NOTICE covering the PureScript
projects it was adapted from.

The implementation differs where Haskell differs. There is no honest reference equality, so
`selectAll` counts every update as a change rather than comparing with `unsafeRefEq`. A
component's initial state is made in its monad, so `connect` reads the store there and the
connected component is in the first render, rather than reading it in an initializer. The store
numbers its updates and a subscriber drops one older than what it already has, because here
updates can come from several threads, or from inside another update's notification, and arrive
out of order. `HalogenM`'s instance lifts with `liftEffect`, which runs at once, since this port's
`lift` is where a program waits. The hooks' `useSelector` is not included.

